From 4212f44eb5fd1a3a8e4e704916c4e12ac9b63a35 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Florian Stosse <florian.stosse@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 13:41:41 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [libc] add sockaddr_in.sin_zero, struct ip_mreq and fd_set
 via sys/types.h

Three definitions that glibc provides in its default mode were missing,
so code that builds with them could not be parsed by Frama-C:

- struct sockaddr_in had no sin_zero[8] padding. Besides
  "Cannot find field sin_zero", it made struct sockaddr_in 8 bytes
  instead of sizeof(struct sockaddr) == 16, so the common idiom
    memset(&sin, 0, sizeof(struct sockaddr));
  got an invalid 'valid_s' precondition from Eva on correct code.
- struct ip_mreq (the argument of IP_ADD_MEMBERSHIP and
  IP_DROP_MEMBERSHIP, whose macros are defined) and struct
  ip_mreq_source (for the *_SOURCE_MEMBERSHIP options) were not defined.
  They are added unguarded, like the other non-POSIX definitions of the
  file: the __USE_MISC/__USE_GNU guard around ip_mreqn is never enabled
  by Frama-C's libc.
- fd_set was not visible after #include <sys/socket.h> alone. glibc's
  <sys/socket.h> includes <sys/types.h>, which includes <sys/select.h>
  in the default (_DEFAULT_SOURCE) mode. Frama-C's <sys/types.h>
  already exposes the other default-mode definitions (u_char, caddr_t),
  so it now includes <sys/select.h>, and <sys/socket.h> includes
  <sys/types.h>.

Oracle changes: struct sockaddr_in is now 16 bytes (tests/libc socket,
socket_h, sys_select), declarations from __fc_select.h are now reached
through sys/select.h (fc_libc, and the list of included headers in six
E-ACSL gen_*.c oracles of builtin/ and format/). New test:
tests/libc/socket_glibc_compat.c.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
